@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] lilly-independent-guest-lifetime
Stopping or restarting the Lilly application, its VM actors, or its console clients MUST
NOT terminate an already running VM or its guest-local terminald PTYs
(ADR-0004, ADR-0017, ADR-0082).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol] lilly-v4-only-execution
Only version 4 provisioner control documents MUST be accepted. Native version 3
intent stores remain independently versioned and MUST preserve existing identity. Execution requires
physical host ownership, image/address validation and confirmed outcomes; durable
receipt alone MUST NOT release resources (ADR-0037, ADR-0017).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lilly-host-utilities-use-argv
Host utility invocations MUST use fixed executable names or validated operator-owned
absolute executables with argument arrays. Peer or guest data MUST NOT become shell
program text (ADR-0013, ADR-0015).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lilly-diagnostics-exclude-secrets
Logs, telemetry metadata, Inspect output and process diagnostic callbacks MUST exclude
provisioner credentials and terminal input/output bytes (ADR-0009, ADR-0020, ADR-0021).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] lilly-no-agent-guests-unattested
A placement whose boot bundle declares `guest_agents` `none` MUST never report a
`guest_ready` fact, MUST record trust as skipped with a receipt bound to the exact
boot instead of delivering trust material, and MUST refuse terminals, workspace
source delivery and the Inception profile. Its running observation comes from the
confined VMM alone (ADR-0170).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] lilly-workspace-source-reference-only
Lilly MUST only hand a validated workspace source reference to the current boot over
its jail vsock socket; the guest runs git. Lilly MUST NOT fetch repositories, write
guest disks, log the reference, or let delivery delay, fail or fence running (ADR-0128).
